## The ruled design (restated)

The prefix-free emission's fold-split rfp moves from `rung_staged` to a NEW
`counts_toward_total=false` ticket list. The split stays emitted, submitted,
staged, compiled, resolvable — manifest, rungs list, reach records, twin
mint, selector inputs all UNCHANGED. The twin keeps riding `rung_staged`,
counted; the twin's Err catch is untouched. The flag's doc law
(`StageTicket::counts_toward_total`) is amended in the same diff to name the
second uncounted class. Count-cut only: no stage-at-commit law changes, no
flattening, nothing deduped away.

## YOUR ONE QUESTION, ANSWERED FIRST — the discriminator

The flip keys on the deferred closure's own `active_cap` parameter:

```rust
active_cap == superdsc::ActiveCap::NONE
```

Line cites:

- **`:11005`** — the deferred closure's signature:
  `active_cap: scratchy_target_spyre::lower_subtile_tape_to_superdsc::ActiveCap`.
  In scope at the classification arm (:11821) unchanged from the closure head.
- **`:13409`** — the ONLY emission call site passing `ActiveCap::NONE`: the
  serial prefix-free ladder. Verified by single-file grep: every other
  ActiveCap-typed call site passes `FULL` or `ActiveCap::decode_ladder(cap)`
  (decode ladder, batch rungs, prefix ladder at :13518, CB at :13655).
- **`:12417-12424`** — the tree's own numeric gate, the pattern this hunk
  mirrors: `Some(_) if active_cap == superdsc::ActiveCap::NONE` selects the
  prefix-free arm of the prefill-mq match.
- **`:12443`** — the tree's own prefix-capable filter:
  `prefill_mq.filter(|_| active_cap == ...ActiveCap::FULL)`.
- **`:12311-12322`** — the tree's own comment naming `ActiveCap::NONE` the
  "PREFIX-FREE PREFILL RUNG" marker and `ActiveCap::FULL` the
  prefix-capable/continuation bundle.

Why this gate cannot uncount a LIVE split:

1. Within a prefix-free emission, the ladder built at :11638-11682 carries
   exactly ONE non-chunk rung — the `(FULL, None, cap)` fold. The 16 chunk
   rungs are caught by the first arm (`rung_chunk.is_some()`), which this
   hunk does not touch.
2. The ceiling rung carrying the PRIMARY body fps is seeded at :11592-11605
   (`decode_rungs = vec![LadderRung { ... bodies: rung_fps(&body_fps) ... }]`)
   BEFORE the ladder loop — the primary bodies never pass through the
   per_rung classification at :11821, so this hunk cannot touch their
   tickets.
3. Prefix-capable emissions pass `ActiveCap::FULL` (:13518) — they never
   enter the new arm; every one of their non-chunk rungs keeps riding
   `rung_staged` counted, fold split included (it serves continuation
   chunks).
4. Decode ladders pass `ActiveCap::decode_ladder(cap)` / `FULL` — same.

